2026-07-30T01:20+02:00 student add-web-first-release-and-monetization 1.0.6 CLOSED, both halves. (a) stale scaffold confirmed: cold `flutter widget-preview start -d chrome` compiles 69 previews with ZERO LucideIcons errors. Correction to the standing rule: this Flutter puts the scaffold under $TMPDIR/flutter_tools.*/widget_preview_scaffold*, NOT .dart_tool/ — that path never existed; the tool self-heals via "Invalid manifest -> Regenerating", `flutter widget-preview clean` is the lever. (b) ROOT CAUSE was never the wasm bytes or the v28 onCreate SQL — preview_db_web.dart called WasmSqlite3.load() without registering any VFS. Native sqlite3 compiles in unix/win32 defaults; the WASM build ships none, and sqlite3_open_v2 resolves a VFS by name on every open (empty name = default), so `:memory:` does NOT exempt it -> SqliteException(1) "no such vfs: " naming the empty string. Fix is one line: registerVirtualFileSystem(InMemoryFileSystem(), makeDefault: true). Second defect found+fixed: _backend() cached the REJECTED future in top-level state, which survives hot reload, so the first failure replayed forever including past the fix — now dropped via onError (residual: mounted States hold late final _future, so only a restart retries). PROVEN: 69 previews compile, zero "no such vfs", zero harness-failed, log shows seeded DB reaching widgets ([MovesDao] watchAll subscribed, MoveList emitted 5 moves / 2 combos); analyze 0/0; suite 1270 pass / 4 skip / 0 fail. NOT PROVEN: how anything LOOKS (owner-gated, no screenshot judged), flutter build web --release, device, live sync. 6.11 ticked, owner sitting -> owner-verification-passes 6.3. Dart MCP registered project-scope in .mcp.json (reports; never judges a look). New: 6.13 (three per-screen exception classes the working harness exposed — battle_intro RenderFlex, missing PartyBloc ancestor, unregistered scene_3d_view on web), 6.14 (two tests flaked once and could NOT be named because the failing run's output was truncated past its own failure blocks; a piped `flutter test | tail` also reports the PIPE's exit code, not the suite's), 1.0.7 (preview_db_web.dart has zero test coverage — conditional exports resolve native under `flutter test`, which is exactly why the green suite said nothing about the broken branch and misdirected 1.0.6 toward the wasm binary).
